abstract: "Reference software and construction-verification materials for HESPN, the Hill Enigma Substitution-Permutation Network. The repository supports an order-eight rotor-scheduled Hill-derived byte-local SPN linear-layer construction. The Enigma name refers only to public stepping among geometric matrix orientations. HESPN is a research harness, not a deployment-ready cipher or a claim that public orientation scheduling improves security over a static layer."
